l need to run all those test cases  which have written multiple times during  your development cycle and doing this  manually definitely is going to be very  tedious and boring and is this effective  of doing it no so what do we do we  automate it so this tells us why we want  to automate one for faster execution two  to be less error prone three to help  frequent execution of our tests so there  were many tools available in the market  for automation one such tool was  selenium and that brings us to the slide  advent of selenium so much before  selenium there are various tools in the  market like rft qtp just to name a few  popular ones the selenium was introduced  by a gentleman called jason huggins way  back in 2004. he was an engineer at  thoughtworks he was kind of working on a  web application which needed frequent  testing and he realized the inefficiency  in doing manual testing of his  application repeatedly so what he did  was he wrote a javascript program that  automatically controlled the browser  actions and then he named that as  javascript test runner he made this open  source which was later renamed as  selenium core and this is how the  selenium came into existence so with  this brief history of selenium let's  understand what the selenium and what  are its main features selenium is the  most popular and widely used automation  tool for automating web applications it  enables us to test web application on  different kind of process like internet  explorer chrome firefox safari opera and  so on and also they introduced support  for edge browser after microsoft  introduced it selenium is a set of tools  and libraries to facilitate automation  of web application it is not a single  tool it has multiple components and  those we will be seeing uh in some time  all these tools together help us test  the web application so selenium is open  source and it is platform independent  this is the biggest reason why people  are preferring this tool because it is 